# Rally-X explosion sound -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Ricardo Bittencourt's netlist of Rally-X's explosion sound, which his file says is
# reconstructed from the hand-drawn schematic. It names the noise ICs by position (11A
# CD4006, 11C CD4070, 11D CD4066); the uA741 and the MB3730 it calls U741 and U3730, which
# are at 12E and 12A on the sheet and the assembly drawing. The Namco WSG's audio is fed
# in by MAME at R28 (I_AUDIO), so it is a port here, and the 'BANG' latch bit (12M 74LS259
# Q0 on the sheet) is a port.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/namco/nl_rallyx.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(rallyx). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Ricardo Bittencourt (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/namco/nl_rallyx.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 138: dropped NET_C(VR1.2, GND) -- VR1 is a pot on the sheet, not a resistor: its bottom is grounded and C4 is on its wiper
# line 165: dropped NET_C(R30.2, C4.1) -- the sheet takes C4 from VR1's wiper, not from VR1's top
# line 168: dropped NET_C(U3730.2, C26.1) -- the sheet puts C27 (22uF) on MB3730 pin 2, not C26
# line 171: dropped NET_C(U3730.3, C27.1) -- the sheet puts C26 (220uF) on MB3730 pin 3, not C27
# line 174: dropped NET_C(U3730.6, R70.1, SPK.1) -- took R70.1 out of it: the sheet's Zobel on pin 6 is R69/C32
# line 177: dropped NET_C(U3730.5, R69.1, SPK.2) -- took R69.1 out of it: the sheet's Zobel on pin 5 is R70/C31
#
# Corrected from the Logic Bd I schematic (A082-91385-C000, manual PDF p. 39):
#   parts the sheet draws that MAME does not have: VR1 1K, C25 100uF, C3 0.1uF
#   the sheet: VR1's bottom to ground, its wiper to C4: VR1.3
#   as above: VR1.2 C4.1; U12A.3 C26.1; U12A.5 R70.1; C25.2 C3.2; U12A.5 (SPEAKER_I)
#   the sheet: MB3730 pin 2 to C27 (22uF), pin 3 to C26 (220uF): U12A.2 C27.1
#   the sheet: the Zobel on pin 6 is R69/C32, on pin 5 R70/C31: U12A.6 R69.1
#   the sheet: C25 and C3 decouple the MB3730's +12V: I_V12 C25.1 C3.1
#   the speaker's leads: MB3730 pin 6 to edge pin 19, pin 5 to edge pin W, both 'SPKR': U12A.6 (SPEAKER_M)
# line 160: SPK is not a part -- the speaker, bridged across the amplifier's outputs, which MAME models as an 8 ohm resistor ('assumed 8 ohm')
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): CLOCK(CLK4V), LOGIC_INPUT(I_BANG), VCVS(VDIFF)
#
# Compared with the Logic Bd I schematic, A082-91385-C000 dated 1/9/81 (PDF p. 39 of the
# manual, doc 1cc6c9614736, with p. 40's overlap; the 'fold-out', doc 47826bd174c7, is the
# assembly drawings), on 2026-10-20 -- every net in the file. The noise generator agrees pin
# for pin, including the spare 4070 and 4066 sections, which the sheet does ground as MAME
# does, and C35's grounded end; so do the uA741 stage, the WSG mix and every value. Corrected
# above from the sheet: the MB3730's capacitors and Zobel networks were on each other's pins
# in MAME (pin 2 has C27 22uF and pin 3 C26 220uF; pin 6 has R69/C32 and pin 5 R70/C31), VR1
# is a pot with C4 on its wiper, and C25 and C3 decouple the amplifier's +12V.
#
# The MB3730's pin names (FB on 2, BYPASS on 3) are MAME's model of the part; with the
# capacitors where the sheet puts them, either those names or MAME's placement was wrong,
# and no Fujitsu data sheet has been read to say which. MAME's comment calls C6 'across
# R41'; on the sheet, and in MAME's own connections, it runs from the input node to the
# 741's output. D1 is printed '1S15..' with the last digits filled in, and the assembly
# notes say D1-D5 are 1N914B; MAME's 1S1588 is kept. The CD4xxx supply pins are not drawn;
# +5V and ground on 14 and 7 are assumed.

# part U11A CD4006  (MAME: SR)
# part U11C CD4070  (MAME: XOR)
# part U11D CD4066  (MAME: SW)
# part U12A MB3730  (MAME: U3730)
# part U12E UA741  (MAME: U741)

value R24 470K
value R26 10K
value R27 150K
value R28 10K
value R30 4.7K
value R31 22K
value R39 68K
value R40 47K
value R41 470K
value R69 1.0
value R70 1.0
value VR1 1K
value C3 0.1uF
value C4 0.1uF
value C5 10nF
value C6 10nF
value C7 0.1uF
value C25 100uF
value C26 220uF
value C27 22uF
value C28 47nF
value C29 22uF
value C31 0.1uF
value C32 0.1uF
value C35 1uF
value C36 0.1uF
value D1 1S1588
value D2 1N914
value D3 1N914

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C25.2 C26.2 C27.2 C28.2 C29.2 C3.2 C31.2 C32.2 C35.2 C36.2 C7.2 R31.2 R40.2 U11A.7 U11D.3 U11D.4 U11D.5 U11D.6 U11D.7 U11D.8 U11D.9 U12A.4 U12E.4 VR1.3 U11C.5 U11C.6 U11C.7 U11C.8 U11C.9
net +12V: C25.1 C3.1 C7.1 D3.1 R39.1 U12A.7 U12E.7
net +5V: U11A.14 U11D.11 U11D.14 U11C.13 U11C.14

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port SPEAKER_I: R70.1 U12A.5  # in MAME: VCVS(VDIFF), SPK, not part: the speaker, bridged across the amplifier's outputs, which MAME models as an 8 ohm resistor ('assumed 8 ohm')
port SPEAKER_M: R69.1 U12A.6  # in MAME: VCVS(VDIFF), SPK, not part: the speaker, bridged across the amplifier's outputs, which MAME models as an 8 ohm resistor ('assumed 8 ohm')
wire C26.1 U12A.3
wire C27.1 U12A.2
wire C4.1 VR1.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4V clock into the shift register
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port CLK4V: U11A.3  # in MAME: CLOCK(CLK4V)
wire U11A.1 U11A.12 U11D.13 U11C.2
wire U11A.8 U11C.1
wire D2.2 U11C.11
wire D2.1 R26.1 U11A.4
wire R26.2 U11C.3
wire U11A.13 U11A.5
wire U11A.10 U11A.6
wire D1.2 R24.1 U11A.9
wire C36.1 D1.1 R24.2 U11C.12
wire C35.1 U11D.1 U11D.10
wire R27.1 U11D.2
wire C5.1 C6.1 R27.2 R31.1
port BANG: U11D.12  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_BANG)
wire C5.2 R41.1 U12E.2
wire C6.2 R30.1 R41.2 U12E.6
wire C29.1 D3.2 R39.2 R40.1 U12E.3
wire C28.1 R28.2 R30.2 VR1.1
port AUDIO: R28.1  # in MAME: ANALOG_INPUT(I_AUDIO)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MB3730 BTL power amp (opamp_lib) + bridged speaker
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C4.2 U12A.1
wire C31.1 R70.2
wire C32.1 R69.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins the MAME netlist never mentions. On a real board these are unused outputs, or
# inputs left open or tied in a way MAME did not draw; they are written here so that
# the checker's coverage test still means something for every other pin.
nc U11A.2 U11A.11  # NC D2+4
nc U11C.4 U11C.10  # output output
nc U12E.1 U12E.5 U12E.8  # NULL NULL NC
